==English==

===Etymology===
Respelling and grammatical repurposing of ''[[bags]] [[I]]'', as used to claim something for oneself, for example, ''Bags I have the top bunk!''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-bagsy.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To make a verbal claim to.
#: {{ux|en|I '''bagsy''' the top bunk of the bed.}}
#*{{RQ:Walliams Bad Dad|text=“After you two nearly killed us, I’m going to drive from now on.” <br>“I never get to drive!” huffed Thumbs. <br>“Well, I '''bagsied''' it first!” snapped Fingers. <br>“I will drive!” announced Dad.}}

